Player native stack
-------------------

1. mpv and Android JNI binding

   Source: https://github.com/Riteshp2001/mpvlibAndroid
   Fixed tag: 2026-06-25
   Fixed commit: 168e0a5e43b37c85509050cddcb5eaddc2e313c0
   Binary input: mpv-android-lib-2026-06-25.aar
   Binary SHA-256: CA0D1C60DDFE5BAD46C369D0D0BF6C2D1A8BB5EC5A3AB916C33F892D0263A75E
   mpv source: https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv

   Kiyori creates a deterministic arm64 player AAR from that fixed input. It
   retains the Java API, required assets, libmpv.so, libplayer.so, the matching
   libc++_shared.so, and the seven FFmpeg libraries built with mpv. To keep
   those HTTPS-capable FFmpeg libraries isolated from the application's
   FFmpegKit tools, Kiyori rewrites only their equal-length ELF SONAME and
   DT_NEEDED strings and stores them as libmpcodec.so, libmpdevice.so,
   libmpfilter.so, libmpformat.so, libmputil.so, libmpresample.so, and
   libmpscale.so. The native machine code and symbol implementations are not
   replaced. Distribution must provide the complete corresponding source,
   transformation script, and build information required by the applicable
   mpv, FFmpeg, Mbed TLS, and GPL licenses.

   Player AAR SHA-256: FC983B7ED0C8B8BE1938283FE94108DFDC593AA31608D55DD1CE119AE201C32C

   C++ runtime SHA-256: C4C2FE5CBCB1FBA0003A31FC7AB29A9BB12DF6CC187EC45A806462540E83D93B
   C++ runtime source: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/tree/main/libcxx
