   preserves the fixed upstream build identity and corresponding-source
   obligation.

3. FFmpegKit Maintained and FFmpeg

   Maven coordinate: dev.ffmpegkit-maintained:ffmpeg-kit-full:8.1.7
   Source: https://github.com/ffmpegkit-maintained/ffmpeg
   Fixed tag: v8.1.7
   Fixed tag object/commit: 62b07bf097baf26b416c815aea514e05c9ad6d63
   Binary SHA-256: C3CBC81D498175FD2AA69EE2DFE7DAFBF519052A96283C2568FE5B3B16618456
   FFmpeg version: n8.1.2

   Kiyori creates a deterministic arm64 tools AAR from this fixed input. It retains
   the Java API, proguard metadata, embedded res/raw license and source notices,
   and the nine FFmpegKit/FFmpeg libraries. It removes the x86_64 libraries and
   the input AAR's C++ runtime so the APK contains the matching mpv runtime
   described above. These normal libav*.so names remain owned by FFmpegKit
   utilities in the main process; the :player process resolves only the
   namespaced mpv FFmpeg closure.

   Tools arm64 AAR SHA-256: 1A30A94226BF2157927EC6EDBB20154F9A1C1C53580F59CF55EFE46DB87A5AB3

   FFmpeg and enabled external libraries retain their own licenses.
   Distribution must provide relinkable/dynamically linked library materials
   and corresponding source as required by LGPL-3.0 and each enabled library's
   notice.

